{"name":"Prosecco","hex":"#fad6a5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Prosecco","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A variety of white grape grown in the Veneto region of Italy."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dry, slightly sparkling Italian white wine made from that grape; also a geographical indication."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Prosecco"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prosecco","blocks":[{"text":"Prosecco is an Italian DOC or DOCG white wine produced in a large area spanning nine provinces in the Veneto and Friuli-Venezia Giulia regions, and named after the village of Prosecco, in the province of Trieste, Italy. It is made from the Prosecco grape, but denomination rules allow up to 15% of the wine to be other permitted varieties. Prosecco is almost always made in sparkling or semi-sparkling style, but a still wine is also permitted. Within the larger designation are two small DOCG areas, Conegliano Valdobbiadene Prosecco in the hills between the comuni (municipalities) of Conegliano and Valdobbiadene, and Asolo Prosecco around the nearby comune of Asolo. Prosecco Superiore is always spumante and comes only from these DOCG areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Prosecco_di_Conegliano_bottle_and_glass.jpg/330px-Prosecco_di_Conegliano_bottle_and_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prosecco"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Cover_Page_Il_Roccolo_Ditirambo_by_Aureliano_Acanti_%281754%29.jpg/330px-Cover_Page_Il_Roccolo_Ditirambo_by_Aureliano_Acanti_%281754%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Cover_Page_Il_Roccolo_Ditirambo_by_Aureliano_Acanti_%281754%29.jpg/330px-Cover_Page_Il_Roccolo_Ditirambo_by_Aureliano_Acanti_%281754%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The cover of the book Il Roccolo Ditirambo (1754), containing for the first time the exact word Prosecco","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACover_Page_Il_Roccolo_Ditirambo_by_Aureliano_Acanti_(1754).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/First_verses_with_word_Prosecco.jpg/500px-First_verses_with_word_Prosecco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/First_verses_with_word_Prosecco.jpg/500px-First_verses_with_word_Prosecco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The poem where the term Prosecco appears for the first time within Il Roccolo Ditirambo (1754), growing on the hill of Monte Berico in Vicenza","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFirst_verses_with_word_Prosecco.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Monte_Berico_dalla_Basilica_Palladiana.jpg/500px-Monte_Berico_dalla_Basilica_Palladiana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Monte_Berico_dalla_Basilica_Palladiana.jpg/1280px-Monte_Berico_dalla_Basilica_Palladiana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Monte_Berico_dalla_Basilica_Palladiana.jpg/500px-Monte_Berico_dalla_Basilica_Palladiana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Monte Berico's hill in Vicenza (UNESCO), where the first described prosecco was growing","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonte_Berico_dalla_Basilica_Palladiana.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Pentagono_del_Cartizze_01.jpg/500px-Pentagono_del_Cartizze_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&